<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · British Isles</p><h1 class="st-title">Lordship of Sligo</h1><p class="st-meta">1384 CE – 1585 CE (approx.) · capital Sligo</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The lordship of the O'Connor Sligo, a branch of the royal O'Connors of Connacht, who ruled northern Connacht from Sligo Castle.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ua-conchobair-dynasty">O'Connors</a> of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-connacht">Connacht</a> divided in 1384 into O'Connor Don and O'Connor Roe, while <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oconnor-sligo">O'Connor Sligo</a>, a separate branch descended from Brian Luighnech, controlled Lower Connacht, centred on the town and castle of Sligo.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oconnor-sligo">O'Connor Sligo</a> ruled over lesser lords such as the O'Haras, O'Dowds and MacDonaghs, frequently contesting the area with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odonnell-dynasty">O'Donnells</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-tir-chonaill">Kingdom of Tir Chonaill</a>, who often claimed overlordship of Sligo. The town held a Dominican friary and was a busy harbour.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/composition-of-connacht">Composition of Connacht</a> in 1585, Sir Donal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oconnor-sligo">O'Connor Sligo</a> accepted English tenure. The family's power waned, and their estates were largely lost after the 17th century wars.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1384 CE – 1585 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">British Isles</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:87.24%;width:4.00%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1384 CE – 1585 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Sligo</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Donal O'Connor Sligo</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Irish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/ireland">Ireland</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>O Connor Sligo, Lower Connacht</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1484&amp;focus=lordship-of-sligo" aria-label="Lordship of Sligo on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4493 317 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Lordship of Sligo lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4813 573L4861 599"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4861 599h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4813 573h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4813 573h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Sligo. <a href="/atlas?year=1484&amp;focus=lordship-of-sligo">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
